From 88bcef76bfbba89ae17429a5fe725c5a3227c6df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joanne Koong <joannelkoong@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 22:28:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: re-lock request before returning from fuse_ref_folio()
References: CVE-2026-53388 bsc#1271825 CVE-2026-64266 bsc#1273555
Git-commit: b5befa80fdbe287a98480effed9564712924add5
Patch-mainline: v7.2-rc1

fuse_ref_folio() unlocks the request but does not re-lock it before
returning. fuse_chan_abort() can end the request and the async end
callback (eg fuse_writepage_free()) can free the args while the
subsequent copy chain logic after fuse_ref_folio() accesses them,
leading to use-after-free issues.

Fix this by locking the request in fuse_ref_folio() before returning.

Fixes: c3021629a0d8 ("fuse: support splice() reading from fuse device")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Joanne Koong <joannelkoong@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Miklos Szeredi <mszeredi@redhat.com>
Acked-by: David Disseldorp <ddiss@suse.de>
---
 fs/fuse/dev.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/fuse/dev.c b/fs/fuse/dev.c
index b230b9a0d3caa..fd8f8201e5599 100644
--- a/fs/fuse/dev.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/dev.c
@@ -974,7 +974,7 @@ static int fuse_ref_page(struct fuse_copy_state *cs, struct page *page,
 	cs->nr_segs++;
 	cs->len = 0;
 
-	return 0;
+	return lock_request(cs->req);
 }
 
